      "title": "Stepwise Trend Sum",
      "topics": [],
      "fastest": true,
      "reverse": false,
      "shortest": true,
      "solution": "n = int(input())\nnums = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\ntotal = 0\nfor i in range(1, n):\n    if nums[i] > nums[i - 1]:\n        total += nums[i]\n    elif nums[i] < nums[i - 1]:\n        total -= nums[i]\n\nprint(total)",
      "statement": "You are given a sequence of [[N]] integers. Process the sequence from left to right while maintaining a running [[total]] initialized to {{0}}.\n\nStarting from the second integer, compare each integer [[X]] with the integer immediately before it:\n- If [[X]] is strictly greater than the previous integer, add [[X]] to [[total]].\n- If [[X]] is strictly less than the previous integer, subtract [[X]] from [[total]].\n- If [[X]] is equal to the previous integer, [[total]] remains unchanged.\n\nOutput the final value of [[total]].",
