    "statementHTML": "<div class=\"statement-body\">\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-goal\">\n   <h2><span class=\"icon icon-goal\">&nbsp;</span><span>Goal </span></h2>\n   <span class=\"question-statement\">You are given a sequence of <var>N</var> integers. Process the sequence from left to right while maintaining a running <var>total</var> initialized to <const>0</const>.<br><br>Starting from the second integer, compare each integer <var>X</var> with the integer immediately before it:<br>- If <var>X</var> is strictly greater than the previous integer, add <var>X</var> to <var>total</var>.<br>- If <var>X</var> is strictly less than the previous integer, subtract <var>X</var> from <var>total</var>.<br>- If <var>X</var> is equal to the previous integer, <var>total</var> remains unchanged.<br><br>Output the final value of <var>total</var>.</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"statement-section statement-protocol\">\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-input\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> An integer <var>N</var>, the number of elements in the sequence.<br><strong>Line 2:</strong> <var>N</var> space-separated integers <var>X</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Output</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-output\"><strong>Line 1:</strong> A single integer representing the final <var>total</var>.</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Constraints</div>\n      <div class=\"question-statement-constraints\">1 &le; <var>N</var> &le; 10<br>-100 &le; <var>X</var> &le; 100</div>\n   </div>\n   <div class=\"blk\">\n      <div class=\"title\">Example</div>\n      <div class=\"statement-inout\">\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-in\">\n            <div class=\"title\">Input</div>\n            <pre class=\"question-statement-example-in\">5\n4 7 7 2 5</pre>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"statement-inout-out\">\n            <div cla